<!--
  ZA.Saga v3.0.0 - intentional API breaks for the major version bump.

  ISagaBuilder carried one boolean per backend, IsEfCoreBackend and IsRedisBackend, with a
  settable mirror on ISagaBuilderMutable and a SetXxxBackend helper for each. That enumerated
  the backends this package knew about, so shipping a new store meant editing the core and
  copying the mutual-exclusion check again. They are replaced by a single HasDurableStore flag
  and SetDurableStore helper; which store is configured comes from SagaStoreRegistrar, which the
  backend installs itself.

  CP0002 covers the eight removed members. CP0006 covers the two added interface members, which
  break existing implementers by design - see the justifications.

  This break is loud: a custom ISagaBuilder fails to compile with a named missing member. The
  other break in v3.0.0 - conflict detection moving from exception type names to
  ISagaConcurrencyConflict - is silent at runtime and is the one to read the release notes for.

  Generated by apicompat in suppression-file mode against the 2.0.4 baseline, then
  annotated. Only the members involved in this change are listed, so an accidental removal
  elsewhere still fails the job.
-->
<Suppressions>
  <Suppression>
    <DiagnosticId>CP0002</DiagnosticId>
    <Target>M:ZeroAlloc.Saga.ISagaBuilder.get_IsEfCoreBackend</Target>
    <Left>lib/net10.0/ZeroAlloc.Saga.dll</Left>
    <Right>lib/net10.0/ZeroAlloc.Saga.dll</Right>
    <IsBaselineSuppression>true</IsBaselineSuppression>
    <Justification>Replaced by HasDurableStore. The flag named one backend while meaning 'a durable store is configured', so every new store had to add a property to this interface.</Justification>
  </Suppression>
